\(x\in A\) means that \(x\) is an element of \(A\); \(A\subseteq B\) means that every element of \(A\) belongs to \(B\). \(\varnothing\) is the empty set.
<ul>
<li>\(A\cap B\): elements belonging to \(A\) <b>and</b> to \(B\);
<li>\(A\cup B\): elements belonging to \(A\) <b>or</b> to \(B\) (possibly both);
<li>in a reference set \(E\), \(\overline A=E\setminus A\) contains the elements of \(E\) that are not in \(A\);
<li>for a finite set, \(\Card(A)\) is its number of elements.
